 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Global sections of the derived internal Hom",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a site whose underlying category is small and $\\mathcal O$ a sheaf of commutative rings on $\\mathcal C$; let $D(\\mathcal O)$ be the derived category [def-weil-abstract-derived-category] of the abelian category of $\\mathcal O$-modules [def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category], and $\\Gamma(\\mathcal C,-)=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal O}(\\mathcal O,-)$ the global sections functor. For $K\\in D(\\mathcal O)$ put $H^0(\\mathcal C,K)=H^0(\\Gamma(\\mathcal C,\\mathcal J^\\bullet))$ for a K-injective complex $\\mathcal J^\\bullet$ [def-pur-kinjective-complex] representing $K$ (one exists by [prop-pur-kinjective-resolutions-exist]; the result does not depend on the choice up to canonical isomorphism, as two K-injective complexes representing $K$ are homotopy equivalent). Then for $L,M\\in D(\\mathcal O)$ there is a canonical isomorphism\n\n$$\n H^0\\bigl(\\mathcal C,R\\mathcal Hom_{\\mathcal O}(L,M)\\bigr)\\cong\\operatorname{Hom}_{D(\\mathcal O)}(L,M),\n$$\n\nwith $R\\mathcal Hom_{\\mathcal O}$ the derived internal Hom [def-pur-derived-internal-hom].",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/sites-cohomology.tex",
  "place": "Lemma 08JA (sites-cohomology-lemma-section-RHom-over-U), the global statement; its proof uses Lemma 0A94 (sites-cohomology-lemma-RHom-into-K-injective) and the lemma sites-cohomology-lemma-RHom-from-K-flat-into-K-injective"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-abstract-derived-category",
  "def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category",
  "def-pur-kinjective-complex",
  "prop-pur-kinjective-resolutions-exist",
  "def-pur-derived-internal-hom",
  "def-pur-ringed-site-zeroth-hypercohomology"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Take the already constructed functorial K-injective replacement I with η: identity → I, using the proved Grothendieck property of module sheaves and the source-library resolution functor. The comparison in [def-pur-derived-internal-hom] computes derivedInternalHom after Q.op.prod Q as Q of Hom(L,I(M)). Apply [lem-pur-hom-complex-hypercohomology] to identify its hypercohomology naturally with homotopy-category Hom(L,I(M)).",
   "uses": [
    "prop-pur-kinjective-resolutions-exist",
    "def-pur-derived-internal-hom",
    "lem-pur-hom-complex-hypercohomology"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply the additive bijection DerivedCategory.Qh.mapAddHom from [lem-weil-pbc-kinjective-hom-derived]. Compose with Iso.homCongr for quotientCompQhIso and with the inverse of Q(η_M) to obtain derived morphisms Q(L) → Q(M). Prove naturality explicitly: Q(I(f)) followed by Q(η) inverse equals Q(η) inverse followed by Q(f), by η.naturality and cancellation. Naturality of quotientCompQhIso transports this equality through the homotopy-to-derived comparison. ULift puts the two abelian-group-valued functors in a common universe.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-weil-pbc-kinjective-hom-derived"
   ],
   "elementary": true
  },
  {
   "text": "Compose the three natural isomorphisms, then descend along the product localization Q.op.prod Q using Localization.fullyFaithfulWhiskeringLeft.preimageIso. Turn the components into additive equivalences and remove the universe lifts. Evaluating the descended naturality square at ULift.up x gives exactly the precomposition/postcomposition equation of rhom_global_sections.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-abstract-derived-category"
   ],
   "elementary": true
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
